00:00:26.153 --> 00:00:28.758
And when you write it down,
it's much more likely to stick

00:00:28.758 --> 00:00:29.816
with yourself too.

00:00:29.816 --> 00:00:31.376
Enjoy.

00:00:31.376 --> 00:00:33.283
- [Robot] Nine,

00:00:33.283 --> 00:00:34.272
eight.

00:00:34.272 --> 00:00:36.855
(hiphop music)

00:00:39.322 --> 00:00:40.877
- So one of the most
difficult things about being

00:00:40.877 --> 00:00:43.971
in a work environment is
being around negative people.

00:00:43.971 --> 00:00:46.658
I think even just in home and in general,

00:00:46.658 --> 00:00:49.023
being around negative
people sucks and being able

00:00:49.023 --> 00:00:51.994
to navigate around and with
those people can sometimes

00:00:51.994 --> 00:00:53.701
be important on your journey.

00:00:53.701 --> 00:00:55.007
And so today I'm going to share with you

00:00:55.007 --> 00:00:57.978
seven different ways to do it
that I hope will inspire you

00:00:57.978 --> 00:00:59.685
and help you on your path.

00:00:59.685 --> 00:01:03.262
(short percussion music)

00:01:03.262 --> 00:01:06.805
My number one way to manage
negative people is don't.

00:01:06.805 --> 00:01:08.613
Don't be around negative people.

00:01:08.613 --> 00:01:10.440
Eliminate them from your life.

00:01:10.440 --> 00:01:13.259
This is what I try to do as
much as possible in my own life.

00:01:13.259 --> 00:01:15.058
This may not be the answer
that you're looking for

00:01:15.058 --> 00:01:18.582
and there's more that are
coming but it's my best answer

00:01:18.582 --> 00:01:21.848
because if you are surrounded
by negative people constantly

00:01:21.848 --> 00:01:24.541
you're going to get more negative,
you're going to be unhappy,

00:01:24.541 --> 00:01:26.014
you're not going to reach your potential.

00:01:26.014 --> 00:01:28.135
And so if I was in a work
environment and this person

00:01:28.135 --> 00:01:30.419
was really negative and
being around me all the time,

00:01:30.419 --> 00:01:31.441
I might try to transfer,

00:01:31.441 --> 00:01:32.916
I might look for other opportunities,

00:01:32.916 --> 00:01:34.596
I might even look at a different company,

00:01:34.596 --> 00:01:36.600
or maybe even leaving and
starting my own business

00:01:36.600 --> 00:01:37.906
and being an entrepreneur.

00:01:37.906 --> 00:01:40.569
If you are an entrepreneur
and you have negative people

00:01:40.569 --> 00:01:43.146
on your team, then that's
an easier decision.

00:01:43.146 --> 00:01:45.436
If somebody is really
skilled and does a great job

00:01:45.436 --> 00:01:47.962
but they're negative, they have to go.

00:01:47.962 --> 00:01:50.010
You cannot be surrounded
by negative people

00:01:50.010 --> 00:01:51.604
because they don't only bring you down,

00:01:51.604 --> 00:01:53.851
they'll bring everybody
else around you down.

00:01:53.851 --> 00:01:56.921
And so you need to have people
who are positive who are

00:01:56.921 --> 00:01:59.417
excited about the project
that you're trying to build.

00:01:59.417 --> 00:02:03.057
(short percussion music)

00:02:03.057 --> 00:02:04.775
My number two technique for
managing negative people

00:02:04.775 --> 00:02:07.181
is to limit your exposure.

00:02:07.181 --> 00:02:09.764
So if you are forced to
deal with negative people,

00:02:09.764 --> 00:02:12.423
I would try to limit how
much exposure I have to them.

00:02:12.423 --> 00:02:15.158
How much time I have to
spend with them would be

00:02:15.158 --> 00:02:18.097
at the bare minimum, just
to get whatever project

00:02:18.097 --> 00:02:19.972
I'm trying to do and get it done.

00:02:19.972 --> 00:02:23.407
And so the first two points
are pretty negative, right?

00:02:23.407 --> 00:02:26.920
It's avoid them, have zero exposure.

00:02:26.920 --> 00:02:29.984
The second one is to limit
your exposure and why?

00:02:29.984 --> 00:02:30.817
You know, if I'm thinking,

00:02:30.817 --> 00:02:32.226
well, I want to be a positive influence,

00:02:32.226 --> 00:02:34.348
I want to help them, I
want to build them up.

00:02:34.348 --> 00:02:36.438
Yes, that's definitely a possibility.

00:02:36.438 --> 00:02:38.727
The reason why I start with
the negative is because

00:02:38.727 --> 00:02:40.973
the opportunity cost is so great.

00:02:40.973 --> 00:02:43.179
For you to spend your
time managing somebody

00:02:43.179 --> 00:02:46.491
who is negative, they will
eat up so much of your time

00:02:46.491 --> 00:02:49.559
and emotional capital and drain you,

00:02:49.559 --> 00:02:51.398
because they're so different than you,

00:02:51.398 --> 00:02:53.603
and getting them to the
place where they can be happy

00:02:53.603 --> 00:02:57.651
is such a big journey that
you could spend that time

00:02:57.651 --> 00:02:59.976
helping 10 other people.

00:02:59.976 --> 00:03:02.555
And so I've always
experienced that the people

00:03:02.555 --> 00:03:06.186
who are negative take the
most work to turn around

00:03:06.186 --> 00:03:09.373
and usually it's not worth
your time compared to

00:03:09.373 --> 00:03:11.216
the other people who you could be helping.

00:03:11.216 --> 00:03:13.306
So that's why my first two
are really negative around

00:03:13.306 --> 00:03:16.211
not being around them at all
or limiting your exposure.

00:03:16.211 --> 00:03:19.719
(short percussion music)

00:03:19.719 --> 00:03:21.392
Alright, now let's jump
to the positive side.

00:03:21.392 --> 00:03:23.563
Number three is be an inspiration.

00:03:23.563 --> 00:03:25.483
So, we have to around
these negative people,

00:03:25.483 --> 00:03:28.592
we have no other option,
they're super important

00:03:28.592 --> 00:03:30.922
and we want to be the force for good.

00:03:30.922 --> 00:03:35.044
You can be an inspiration
to build people up.

00:03:35.044 --> 00:03:38.310
And so I think of when
women first get together

00:03:38.310 --> 00:03:40.766
in an office setting an
eventually their periods

00:03:40.766 --> 00:03:42.809
start to align together.

00:03:42.809 --> 00:03:44.523
That kind of happens with everything.

00:03:44.523 --> 00:03:46.896
If you are around toxic people,

00:03:46.896 --> 00:03:49.347
you're more likely to be
toxic on an ongoing basis.

00:03:49.347 --> 00:03:52.168
If you're around people who
are working out all the time,

00:03:52.168 --> 00:03:54.336
you're more likely to want to work out

00:03:54.336 --> 00:03:55.524
and take care of yourself.

00:03:55.524 --> 00:03:56.714
If you're around complainers,

00:03:56.714 --> 00:03:58.231
you're going to start complaining more.

00:03:58.231 --> 00:03:59.748
And so you become your environment.

00:03:59.748 --> 00:04:01.175
So if you have that awareness,

00:04:01.175 --> 00:04:03.261
you can be an inspiration for that person.

00:04:03.261 --> 00:04:05.586
By them just being around you,

00:04:05.586 --> 00:04:07.300
you are going to pull them up.

00:04:07.300 --> 00:04:10.573
I used to volunteer at a
hospital, Sunnybrook Hospital

00:04:10.573 --> 00:04:14.612
here in Toronto, and one of
my shifts was with this woman

00:04:14.612 --> 00:04:17.475
who was in charge of
the phones on her floor.

00:04:17.475 --> 00:04:19.112
And she would also pick
up the phone in kind of

00:04:19.112 --> 00:04:20.053
very angry way.

00:04:20.053 --> 00:04:22.146
It was, C2 Laura, C2 Laura.

00:04:22.146 --> 00:04:25.089
It was kind of very angry
and it was kind of against

00:04:25.089 --> 00:04:27.793
how I would do things and just
the vibe I wanted to put out.

00:04:27.793 --> 00:04:30.370
And by spending more
and more time with her,

00:04:30.370 --> 00:04:32.377
eventually she got more positive.

00:04:32.377 --> 00:04:35.490
She said, C2 Laura, C2
this is Laura speaking.

00:04:35.490 --> 00:04:38.023
And it slowly got more and more
and more and more positive.

00:04:38.023 --> 00:04:40.994
Now, as I left Sunnybrook,
as my volunteer shift ended,

00:04:40.994 --> 00:04:43.564
I don't know if that
continued or if she fell back

00:04:43.564 --> 00:04:46.872
to her usual path, but
expect that to happen.

00:04:46.872 --> 00:04:48.548
You know, the more they are around you,

00:04:48.548 --> 00:04:50.966
I want you to be a force for good, right?

00:04:50.966 --> 00:04:52.763
When you find your one
word, whatever that is,

00:04:52.763 --> 00:04:56.523
that exudes out of you in
every situation that you go to.

00:04:56.523 --> 00:05:00.211
So if you are around me for
any consistent period of time,

00:05:00.211 --> 00:05:03.403
even from watching the videos,
you're going to believe harder,

00:05:03.403 --> 00:05:05.283
you're going to believe
stronger in yourself,

00:05:05.283 --> 00:05:07.037
in your ideas, in the people around you

00:05:07.037 --> 00:05:08.551
because that's what I'm all about.

00:05:08.551 --> 00:05:10.881
You can't be in my circle

00:05:10.881 --> 00:05:13.623
and not gain a little bit more belief.

00:05:13.623 --> 00:05:14.728
It's just going to happen.

00:05:14.728 --> 00:05:18.206
So that should be you with
your one word getting out there

00:05:18.206 --> 00:05:19.924
and being an inspiration for people.

00:05:19.924 --> 00:05:23.241
The danger is that, as I said,

00:05:23.241 --> 00:05:25.204
two people tend to come together,

00:05:25.204 --> 00:05:28.267
the danger is that you become
more toxic and you become

00:05:28.267 --> 00:05:30.764
more negative so you need
to have enough other stuff

00:05:30.764 --> 00:05:32.926
in your environment that
keeps you at a high level

00:05:32.926 --> 00:05:36.725
that pulls them you instead
of you going to them.

00:05:36.725 --> 00:05:40.282
(short percussion music)

00:05:40.282 --> 00:05:44.043
- Tip number four is to come
from a place of understanding.

00:05:44.043 --> 00:05:46.321
I think a lot of people's
negativity is actually

00:05:46.321 --> 00:05:49.385
deeply rooted into something else beyond

00:05:49.385 --> 00:05:51.179
what they're complaining about.

00:05:51.179 --> 00:05:54.894
So I had a situation with a
negative person on my team.

00:05:54.894 --> 00:05:56.451
They were constantly putting others down.

00:05:56.451 --> 00:05:59.636
They were constantly paranoid
about what the company's

00:05:59.636 --> 00:06:01.188
situation was going to be like.

00:06:01.188 --> 00:06:04.500
And they were also gossiping
a lot and spreading rumors.

00:06:04.500 --> 00:06:06.581
And every single day he would complain.

00:06:06.581 --> 00:06:08.994
I would ask him how his
day's going and he would

00:06:08.994 --> 00:06:10.345
just say it's terrible.

00:06:10.345 --> 00:06:12.426
And it got to a point that
it was actually starting

00:06:12.426 --> 00:06:16.150
to make me feel negative
about my situation at work.

00:06:16.150 --> 00:06:17.545
And then finally I had to have

00:06:17.545 --> 00:06:19.792
a sit down conversation with him.

00:06:19.792 --> 00:06:22.948
I wanted to find out why
he was being so negative.

00:06:22.948 --> 00:06:24.742
Then he revealed to me
that he was paranoid

00:06:24.742 --> 00:06:26.099
of losing his job.

00:06:26.099 --> 00:06:29.695
He would wake up every morning
with a fear that he won't

00:06:29.695 --> 00:06:33.050
be able to feed his family,
he will not be able to go

00:06:33.050 --> 00:06:35.637
on that vacation that
he promised his wife.

00:06:35.637 --> 00:06:38.829
Although I wasn't able to
promise him the job security

00:06:38.829 --> 00:06:42.632
that he wanted, I was able to
provide him with the security

00:06:42.632 --> 00:06:45.295
and safety that he had someone at work

00:06:45.295 --> 00:06:46.561
that he could confide in.

00:06:46.561 --> 00:06:49.340
And little by little, I
started to see more positivity

00:06:49.340 --> 00:06:51.885
come out of him, especially towards me,

00:06:51.885 --> 00:06:54.498
which made my life at work a lot easier.

00:06:54.498 --> 00:06:56.779
So the next time you come
across someone negative,

00:06:56.779 --> 00:06:58.419
before you write them off,

00:06:58.419 --> 00:07:00.709
try to come from a place of understanding.

00:07:00.709 --> 00:07:04.393
(short percussion music)

00:07:04.393 --> 00:07:06.267
- Number five is figure out their dream.

00:07:06.267 --> 00:07:07.980
I like to say that one of
the most dangerous things

00:07:07.980 --> 00:07:10.824
that you can do is tell
me what your dream is.

00:07:10.824 --> 00:07:14.290
If I know what your dream is
then I am always thinking about

00:07:14.290 --> 00:07:18.235
how do I help this person at
this thing that they want to do

00:07:18.235 --> 00:07:20.425
and pushing you to get
past those limited beliefs

00:07:20.425 --> 00:07:23.221
and the negative mindsets to
help you go off and accomplish

00:07:23.221 --> 00:07:24.162
your big thing.

00:07:24.162 --> 00:07:27.968
And so even the most negative
person has some kind of dream.

00:07:27.968 --> 00:07:29.234
They may not feel it's possible,

00:07:29.234 --> 00:07:31.280
they may feel like the
world's against them and that

00:07:31.280 --> 00:07:33.437
people are conspiring to keep them down

00:07:33.437 --> 00:07:36.833
but somewhere deep down
inside they have a dream

00:07:36.833 --> 00:07:38.919
of something that they wan to accomplish.

00:07:38.919 --> 00:07:42.237
And so if you can figure
out what their dream is,

00:07:42.237 --> 00:07:44.683
and then find ways to
help them accomplish it,

00:07:44.683 --> 00:07:46.974
be their friend, be their
accountability partner,

00:07:46.974 --> 00:07:48.488
give them some resources,

00:07:48.488 --> 00:07:50.135
give them some motivational boosts,

00:07:50.135 --> 00:07:52.507
share things with them
to help them lift up

00:07:52.507 --> 00:07:54.956
and get towards that goal,
then it's really hard

00:07:54.956 --> 00:07:57.371
to be making progress towards your dream

00:07:57.371 --> 00:07:59.693
and being negative and
unhappy at the same time.

00:07:59.693 --> 00:08:02.877
And so guiding them along
that path and encouraging them

00:08:02.877 --> 00:08:05.000
will help turn that tide
and turn them from being

00:08:05.000 --> 00:08:07.166
super negative to more positive.

00:08:07.166 --> 00:08:10.732
(short percussion music)

00:08:10.732 --> 00:08:13.228
Number six is recognize
their good behavior.

00:08:13.228 --> 00:08:16.736
This is basic parenting
skills or if you are trying to

00:08:16.736 --> 00:08:19.106
train a dog, it's kind of the same thing.

00:08:19.106 --> 00:08:20.086
You have two options.

00:08:20.086 --> 00:08:21.596
You either punish their bad behavior

00:08:21.596 --> 00:08:24.213
or you recognize their good behavior.

00:08:24.213 --> 00:08:26.013
And you may not be in a
position to punish them

00:08:26.013 --> 00:08:27.809
for their bad behaviors and it may be

00:08:27.809 --> 00:08:30.593
actually what they want
because they seek the attention

00:08:30.593 --> 00:08:32.387
and they love going to a negative place.

00:08:32.387 --> 00:08:34.445
And so if I was dealing
with that kind of person,

00:08:34.445 --> 00:08:37.175
I had to deal with them,
then I'd be looking at

00:08:37.175 --> 00:08:40.024
the negative stuff I'm
just going to ignore

00:08:40.024 --> 00:08:43.088
and anytime there is something
positive that they do for me

00:08:43.088 --> 00:08:45.371
or the mindset that they have
or something that they shared

00:08:45.371 --> 00:08:47.578
that was happy, or funny, or positive,

00:08:47.578 --> 00:08:50.923
I would go all in on
encouraging that and thank them

00:08:50.923 --> 00:08:52.110
and appreciate them.

00:08:52.110 --> 00:08:53.293
Not in a fake way.

00:08:53.293 --> 00:08:55.616
Not in a way that they see,
obviously, right through

00:08:55.616 --> 00:08:58.885
but in the genuine way
of you really connecting

00:08:58.885 --> 00:09:01.585
to that thing that they did
for you and thanking them,

00:09:01.585 --> 00:09:04.329
maybe buying them a little
cupcake or something

00:09:04.329 --> 00:09:06.127
as a show of appreciation.

00:09:06.127 --> 00:09:08.660
Because negative people
aren't surrounded by a lot

00:09:08.660 --> 00:09:10.419
of positivity in general.

00:09:10.419 --> 00:09:12.387
It's how the become so negative.

00:09:12.387 --> 00:09:15.773
And so buy you recognizing
the good deeds that they did,

00:09:15.773 --> 00:09:18.493
giving them some appreciation,
giving them some rewards,

00:09:18.493 --> 00:09:21.449
they're going to want to do
it again and again and again

00:09:21.449 --> 00:09:23.121
and lift out of that negativity.

00:09:23.121 --> 00:09:26.838
(short percussion music)

00:09:26.838 --> 00:09:29.044
And my number seven way to
deal with negative people

00:09:29.044 --> 00:09:32.028
is help them find a happier place.

00:09:32.028 --> 00:09:34.566
Quite often, negative
people are so bummed out

00:09:34.566 --> 00:09:36.079
by their position, by their work,

00:09:36.079 --> 00:09:37.469
they're not passionate about it anymore,

00:09:37.469 --> 00:09:39.758
they don't, you know, have
the desire to be there anymore

00:09:39.758 --> 00:09:42.984
and everybody would be
happier if they moved on.

00:09:42.984 --> 00:09:44.864
It kind of ties a little
bit into understanding

00:09:44.864 --> 00:09:47.601
what their dream is because
often if they have a dream

00:09:47.601 --> 00:09:49.563
and they're doing something
totally different,

00:09:49.563 --> 00:09:51.425
then they're going to
be negative and unhappy.

00:09:51.425 --> 00:09:52.988
They're going to see
other people who are off

00:09:52.988 --> 00:09:54.782
accomplishing these
great things in the field

00:09:54.782 --> 00:09:57.967
that they want to be in and
they're stuck in this job

00:09:57.967 --> 00:09:58.822
that they hate.

00:09:58.822 --> 00:10:01.885
And so helping push them
to follow that dream,

00:10:01.885 --> 00:10:05.031
find a happier place,
go pursue that passion,

00:10:05.031 --> 00:10:06.740
is great for them because they're happier,

00:10:06.740 --> 00:10:08.135
they're off doing the thing that they need

00:10:08.135 --> 00:10:10.139
and sometimes they just
need a little bit of a push.

00:10:10.139 --> 00:10:11.935
And it's great for you because
now you don't have to deal

00:10:11.935 --> 00:10:14.592
with this negative person in
your work environment anymore.

00:10:14.592 --> 00:10:15.633
So those are my top seven ways

00:10:15.633 --> 00:10:17.715
on how to manage negative people at work.

00:10:17.715 --> 00:10:19.511
I'd love to know what did you guys think?

00:10:19.511 --> 00:10:20.656
What was your favorite one?

00:10:20.656 --> 00:10:21.918
Which one really hit home?

00:10:21.918 --> 00:10:24.324
